# --- toolkit: hr_assistant -------------------------------------------------
# Five HR tools over deterministic seed data, inlined into the generated agent.
#
# Vendored from the AWS-published sample
#   awslabs/amazon-bedrock-agentcore-samples
#   01-features/06-observe-evaluate-optimize-your-agent/03-optimize/utils/hr_assistant_agent.py
# reduced to seed data + the five @tool functions. Everything the sample carries
# below its tools — BedrockAgentCoreApp, BedrockModel("us.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0"),
# the session cache, its own entrypoint and its own config-bundle read — is owned
# by the surrounding Launchpad template instead. In particular the model is NOT
# hardcoded here: the template honours the spec's model_id / model_source.
#
# The docstrings are VERBATIM from the sample, including the Args sections. They
# are the tool descriptions the model sees (strands strips only Args) and the
# input-schema parameter descriptions, i.e. exactly the surface a tool-description
# A/B experiment varies. Do not "improve" them.
#
# ONE deliberate deviation: the sample numbers PTO requests from a module-level
# counter, so the same prompt returns a different request_id on every call. This
# toolkit derives the number from the request arguments instead, so a given prompt
# always yields the same tool result. Format and docstring are unchanged.

